          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775306922637_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1775306922637_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict JSON emitter.\n\nTask: Convert the input negotiation table text into a JSON array of issue rows.\n\nCRITICAL JSON RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n1. Output MUST be valid JSON.\n2. Output MUST start with `[` and end with `]`.\n3. Output ONLY JSON. No markdown, no prose, no backticks, no code fences.\n4. Use double quotes for all keys and string values.\n5. No trailing commas.\n6. Do not output NaN, undefined, or comments.\n7. If extraction is uncertain or no valid rows are found, output `[]` exactly.\n\nCOLUMN INDEX INTEGRITY (MANDATORY):\n- Lock column mapping from the header row by physical column position (A, B, C...).\n- Never shift values left/right when a cell is blank.\n- If Original Clause column cell is blank for a row, keep original_clause = null even if adjacent Supplier column has value.\n- Supplier/Buyer fields must be filled only from their mapped header columns, not from nearest non-empty cell.\n\nCONTRACT CONTEXT\n- BuyOrSell flag:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES.$output.result.BuyOrSell}}\n- If BuyOrSell = \"B\": negotiation is between SUPPLIER and BUYER. Latest CR should come from SUPPLIER side.\n- If BuyOrSell = \"S\": negotiation is between CUSTOMER and SUPPLIER. Treat CUSTOMER as BUYER for output fields. Latest CR should come from CUSTOMER side (i.e., buyer-side fields in output).\n\nROW RULES\n- Treat the first meaningful row as headers.\n- Ignore separator/decorative/summary rows.\n- Keep only rows that represent negotiation issues.\n- Headers are NOT fixed. Do NOT rely only on patterns like `Supplier 1/Buyer 1/Supplier 2/Buyer 2`.\n- Detect role columns from header semantics, including variants such as:\n  - Supplier Request, Supplier Response, Supplier Comment, Vendor Request/Response\n  - Buyer Request, Buyer Response, Buyer Comment\n  - Customer Request, Customer Response, Customer Comment\n  - Counterparty Request/Response (infer side from context if possible)\n- Detect rounds from header text when present, including forms like:\n  - `R1`, `R2`, `Round 1`, `Round-2`, `(R3)`, `Supplier 2`, `Buyer 2`, `Customer 2`\n- If round is not explicit, infer stable ascending order from column position among same-side conversation columns.\n- If supplier or buyer request is available, then latest_supplier_message/latest_supplier_message MUST be filled with that in output\n- Treat supplier or buyer request raw column as supplier or buyer request column only. DONT treat it as original_clause_text\n\nFor each valid row, emit ALL keys below:\n- id\n- status\n- clause_number\n- clause_name\n- original_clause\n- reason\n- supplier_message\n- buyer_message\n- latest_supplier_message (Must if latest supplier request is present)\n- latest_buyer_message (Must if latest buyer request is present)\n- supplier_messages (array ordered by round asc, non-empty only)\n- buyer_messages (array ordered by round asc, non-empty only)\n- round_messages (array of objects: {\"round\": number, \"supplier_message\": string|null, \"buyer_message\": string|null})\n- raw_columns (object with normalized header->value for every non-empty column in the row)\n\nNORMALIZATION\n- Map header names case-insensitively.\n- Normalize headers to snake_case.\n- Trim whitespace.\n- Empty cells => null.\n- If status missing => \"\".\n- For clause_name: convert any newlines/carriage returns/tabs to a single space, collapse repeated spaces, and trim.\n- clause_name MUST be a single-line string (never include `\\n` or `\\r`).\n- Treat CUSTOMER columns as BUYER-side for output (`buyer_*` fields).\n- `supplier_messages` must contain supplier-side messages only, ordered by round asc.\n- `buyer_messages` must contain buyer/customer-side messages only, ordered by round asc.\n- `round_messages` must merge both sides per round where possible.\n- `latest_supplier_message` MUST be the highest-round non-empty supplier-side message.\n- `latest_buyer_message` MUST be the highest-round non-empty buyer/customer-side message.\n- `supplier_message` MUST equal `latest_supplier_message`.\n- `buyer_message` MUST equal `latest_buyer_message`.\n- If only one side has explicit rounds and the other does not, still preserve ascending order and align best-effort by round index.\n- If only one supplier or buyer/customer column exists, use that value as latest for that side.\n\nVALIDATION / FALLBACK\n- Do not invent issue rows.\n- If required issue rows cannot be reliably extracted, return `[]`.\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$nodes.NEGOTIATION_FEEDBACK_DOCUMENT.$output.text}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1777000001001",
          "code": "VALIDATE_NEGOTIATION_HEADERS_AND_VALUES",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Validate Negotiation Headers and Values",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const buyOrSell = (($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES?.$output?.result?.BuyOrSell) || '').toString().trim().toUpperCase();\nconst contractType = (($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES?.$output?.result?.ContractTypeName) || '').toString().trim();\nconst fileName = (($context.$variables?.fileName) || '').toString().trim();\nconst raw = $context.$nodes.NEGOTIATION_JSON_DATA?.$output;\n\nconst rows = Array.isArray(raw)\n  ? raw\n  : (raw && Array.isArray(raw.result) ? raw.result : []);\n\nconst normalizeHeader = (v) => (v == null ? '' : v.toString().trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '_').replace(/^_+|_+$/g, ''));\nconst foldHeader = (v) => normalizeHeader(v).replace(/_/g, '');\nconst toText = (v) => (v == null ? '' : v.toString().trim());\nconst unique = (arr) => Array.from(new Set((arr || []).filter(Boolean)));\n\nconst buildNegotiationValidationEmail = (sections) => {\n  const fileLabel = fileName || 'uploaded_file';\n  const typeLabel = contractType || 'selected contract type';\n  const esc = (v) => String(v ?? '')\n    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')\n    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')\n    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')\n    .replace(/\"/g, '&quot;')\n    .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');\n\n  let message = '';\n  message += '<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.5;color:#111;\">';\n  message += '<p>Hi,</p>';\n  message += '<p>Your recent file upload <strong>' + esc(fileLabel) + '</strong> could not be processed due to validation errors. Please review the details below and correct the file before re-uploading.</p>';\n  message += '<h3>Summary of Issues</h3>';\n  message += '<p>The uploaded file does not match the required format for the selected contract type.</p>';\n  message += '<hr/>';\n  message += '<h3>What Needs Attention</h3>';\n\n  let sectionIndex = 1;\n  for (const section of sections) {\n    if (!section) continue;\n    message += '<p><strong>' + sectionIndex + '. ' + esc(section.title) + '</strong></p>';\n\n    for (const lineRaw of section.lines || []) {\n      const line = String(lineRaw || '').replace('{{contract_type}}', typeLabel);\n      message += '<p>' + esc(line) + '</p>';\n    }\n\n    const bullets = Array.isArray(section.bullets) ? section.bullets : [];\n    if (bullets.length > 0) {\n      message += '<ul>';\n      for (const itemRaw of bullets) {\n        const item = String(itemRaw || '').replace('{{contract_type}}', typeLabel);\n        message += '<li>' + esc(item) + '</li>';\n      }\n      message += '</ul>';\n    }\n\n    sectionIndex += 1;\n  }\n\n  message += '<hr/>';\n  message += '<h3>Required Fields</h3>';\n  message += '<ul>';\n  message += '<li>ID</li>';\n  message += '<li>Status</li>';\n  message += '<li>Clause Name</li>';\n  message += '<li>At least one of Supplier_X or Customer_X</li>';\n  message += '</ul>';\n  message += '<hr/>';\n  message += '<h3>Next Steps</h3>';\n  message += '<ol>';\n  message += '<li>Download the latest template</li>';\n  message += '<li>Update your file to match the required format</li>';\n  message += '<li>Ensure all mandatory fields are populated</li>';\n  message += '<li>Re-upload the corrected file</li>';\n  message += '</ol>';\n  message += '<hr/>';\n  message += '<p>If the issue persists, please contact support with your file and contract type details.</p>';\n  message += '</div>';\n\n  return message;\n};\n\nif (!Array.isArray(rows) || rows.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error(buildNegotiationValidationEmail([\n    {\n      title: 'Negotiation Data Missing',\n      lines: [\n        'No negotiation data was found in the uploaded file.',\n        'Please ensure the file contains issue rows in the expected template format for contract type {{contract_type}}.'\n      ]\n    }\n  ]));\n}\n\nconst requiredAlways = ['id', 'status', 'clause_name'];\nconst anyOfBySide = {\n  B: ['latest_supplier_message', 'original_clause_text', 'supplier_message', 'reason', 'round_messages'],\n  S: ['latest_buyer_message', 'original_clause_text', 'buyer_message', 'reason', 'round_messages']\n};\n\nconst anyOfHeaders = anyOfBySide[buyOrSell];\nif (!anyOfHeaders) {\n  throw new Error(buildNegotiationValidationEmail([\n    {\n      title: 'Contract Setup Incomplete',\n      lines: [\n        'Contract setup is incomplete for contract type {{contract_type}}.',\n        'BuyOrSell configuration is missing or invalid, so request-side validation could not be determined.'\n      ]\n    }\n  ]));\n}\n\nconst firstRow = rows[0] || {};\nconst headerMapByFold = {};\nfor (const key of Object.keys(firstRow)) {\n  const fk = foldHeader(key);\n  if (fk && !headerMapByFold[fk]) {\n    headerMapByFold[fk] = key;\n  }\n}\n\nconst getActualKey = (requiredHeader) => headerMapByFold[foldHeader(requiredHeader)] || null;\n\nconst hasMeaningfulValue = (row, headerName) => {\n  const actualKey = getActualKey(headerName);\n  if (!actualKey) return false;\n\n  const rawValue = row?.[actualKey];\n  const normalizedHeader = foldHeader(headerName);\n\n  if (normalizedHeader === 'roundmessages') {\n    if (Array.isArray(rawValue)) return rawValue.length > 0;\n    if (typeof rawValue === 'string') {\n      const text = rawValue.trim();\n      if (!text || text === '[]') return false;\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(text);\n        if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return parsed.length > 0;\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return true;\n    }\n    return !!toText(rawValue);\n  }\n\n  return !!toText(rawValue);\n};\n\nconst missingHeaders = [];\nrequiredAlways.forEach((h) => {\n  if (!getActualKey(h)) missingHeaders.push(h);\n});\n\nconst availableAnyHeaders = anyOfHeaders.filter((h) => !!getActualKey(h));\nif (availableAnyHeaders.length === 0) {\n  missingHeaders.push(...anyOfHeaders);\n}\n\nconst missingFieldNames = [];\nrows.forEach((row) => {\n  requiredAlways.forEach((h) => {\n    const actualKey = getActualKey(h);\n    const val = toText(actualKey ? row?.[actualKey] : '');\n    if (!val) missingFieldNames.push(h);\n  });\n\n  const anyFilled = availableAnyHeaders.some((h) => hasMeaningfulValue(row, h));\n  if (!anyFilled) {\n    missingFieldNames.push('supplier_x or customer_x');\n  }\n});\n\nconst finalMissingHeaders = unique(missingHeaders);\nconst finalMissingFields = unique(missingFieldNames);\nconst hasHeaderIssue = finalMissingHeaders.length > 0;\nconst hasFieldIssue = finalMissingFields.length > 0;\n\nif (hasHeaderIssue || hasFieldIssue) {\n  const sections = [];\n\n  if (hasHeaderIssue) {\n    sections.push({\n      title: 'Missing or Incorrect Column Headers',\n      lines: [\n        'Following required columns are missing or incorrectly named.',\n        'Ensure headers exactly match the template (including underscores).'\n      ],\n      bullets: finalMissingHeaders\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (hasFieldIssue) {\n    sections.push({\n      title: 'Mandatory Fields Not Populated',\n      lines: [\n        'Following Mandatory fields contain empty or invalid values for the contract type {{contract_type}}.',\n        'All mandatory fields must be completed for every row.'\n      ],\n      bullets: finalMissingFields\n    });\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(buildNegotiationValidationEmail(sections));\n}\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  node: 'VALIDATE_NEGOTIATION_HEADERS_AND_VALUES',\n  event: 'mandatory_headers_and_values_validated',\n  buyOrSell,\n  rowCount: rows.length,\n  requiredAlways,\n  anyOfHeaders,\n  availableAnyHeaders\n}));\n\nreturn rows;",
            "description": "Validates Negotiation Data",
            "errorNodeId": "1777880008938"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5240,
            "y": 6316
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776503054827"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1776503054827",
          "code": "GET_CLAUSE_TITLES_FROM_NEGOTIATIONS",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Gets the clause titles from negotiation JSON",
            "name": "Get clause titles from negotiations",
            "sourceType": "code",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const raw = $context.$nodes.VALIDATE_NEGOTIATION_HEADERS_AND_VALUES?.$output.result;\n\nconst rows = Array.isArray(raw)\n  ? raw\n  : (raw && Array.isArray(raw.result) ? raw.result : []);\n\nconst toText = (v) => (v == null ? '' : v.toString().trim());\n\nconst clauseTitles = [];\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const title = toText(row?.clause_name);\n  if (title) clauseTitles.push(title);\n}\n\nreturn clauseTitles;",
            "errorNodeId": "1777879914368"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5258,
            "y": 6538
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776503962395"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1776503962395",
          "code": "LOOP_OVER_CLAUSE_TITLES",
          "type": "LOOP",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Loops over clause titles",
