                              "name": "prompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": "You are a rule matcher system.\n\nYour task is to compare the Change Request with the CURRENT rule row only and decide whether the Change Request belongs to this rule row.\n\nINPUT\n1. Change request row JSON (CONTEXT ONLY - NOT authoritative for matching decision)\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem}}\n\n2. Authoritative change request text (already resolved by perspective and latest non-empty side message):\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.active_change_request_text}}\n\n3. Current policy rule row (JSON format)\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_POLICY_IN_POLICY_JSON.$currentItem}}\n\nAUTHORITATIVE SOURCE CONTROL\n- The only request text allowed for deciding rule_found/rule_id/match_score/match_type is input #2 (authoritative change request text).\n- Input #1 (full row JSON) is context only for background (clause title, thread context, metadata).\n- Never use any message/request fields from input #1 as evidence for matching, including supplier_message, buyer_message, latest_supplier_message, latest_buyer_message, reason, raw_columns, or any derived fields.\n- If input #1 conflicts with input #2, follow input #2.\n\nINTENT-FIRST MATCHING RULES\n- Use ONLY the authoritative change request text above for matching.\n- Do not use older same-side requests when a later non-empty request exists.\n- Ignore formatting noise during comparison: newlines, tabs, repeated spaces, and non-alphanumeric symbols.\n- Match by policy topic/intent first (rule_description + position semantics), not by identical wording.\n- Topic alignment determines row eligibility.\n- Numeric/value differences DO NOT disqualify row eligibility when topic aligns.\n- Numeric/value differences are evaluated later for position outcome (e.g., OUT_OF_POLICY), not here.\n\nDOMAIN EXAMPLE (MANDATORY INTERPRETATION)\n- If request says: \"PBG should be 250,000 USD\" or \"PBG 10%\" and current rule topic is \"PBG amount\", then this row IS a match.\n- It may still be OUT_OF_POLICY later, but rule_found here should be true.\n\nDISQUALIFIER\n- If current row topic is different (example: \"PBG validity days\") while request is about amount/value, then no_match.\n\nIDENTIFIER RULE\n- If rule_found is true, rule_id MUST be populated.\n- Use current row identifier in this order: rule_id, else rule_code, else id.\n\nReturn:\n- rule_found: true if the Change Request fits this rule row\n- rule_id: row identifier if found\n- match_score: a number from 0 to 1\n- match_type: exact / semantic / partial / no_match\n\nScoring priority:\n1. scenario / intent match\n2. clause meaning match\n3. numeric value / threshold / condition match\n\nOUTPUT JSON ONLY\n\nIf matched:\n{\n  \"rule_found\": true,\n  \"rule_id\": \"<row identifier>\",\n  \"match_score\": 0.92,\n  \"match_type\": \"semantic\"\n}\n\nIf not matched:\n{\n  \"rule_found\": false,\n  \"rule_id\": null,\n  \"match_score\": 0,\n  \"match_type\": \"no_match\"\n}"
                            },
                            {
                              "id": "1775367260657_systemPrompt",
                              "name": "systemPrompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": ""
                            }
                          ],
                          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rule_found\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n    \"rule_id\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n    \"match_score\": { \"type\": \"number\" },\n    \"match_type\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"rule_found\", \"match_score\", \"match_type\"]\n}"
                        },
                        {
