                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1775546372124",
                  "code": "GET_THE_CLAUSE_TEXT",
                  "type": "CODE",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Get the Clause Text",
                    "sourceCode": "const normalize = (v) => (v || '').toString().toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n\nconst row = $context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem || {};\nconst rawTitle = row.clause_name || '';\nconst clauseTitle = normalize(rawTitle);\n\nconst clausesArray = $context.$nodes.AGGREGATE_FETCHED_CLAUSES.$output.result || [];\n\nconst matchedClause = clausesArray.find((c) => {\n  const t = normalize(c?.clause_title);\n  if (!clauseTitle || !t) return false;\n  return t === clauseTitle || t.includes(clauseTitle) || clauseTitle.includes(t);\n});\n\nconst clauseText = matchedClause ? matchedClause.clause_text : null;\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  node: 'GET_THE_CLAUSE_TEXT',\n  event: 'clause_text_resolved',\n  issueNumber: row.id ?? row.issue_id ?? row.issue_number ?? null,\n  rawTitle,\n  normalizedTitle: clauseTitle,\n  found: !!matchedClause,\n  mappedTitle: matchedClause?.clause_title ?? null,\n  clauseTextLength: clauseText ? clauseText.length : 0\n}));\n\nreturn clauseText;",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "description": "Looks up and returns the original clause text for the current clause number from the clause-text map.",
                    "errorNodeId": "1777879914368"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 5295.5,
                    "y": 14987
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1775380208478"
                  },
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1775380208478",
                  "code": "DETERMINE_CHANGE_REQUEST_POSITION",
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Determine Change Request Position",
                    "description": "Determines whether the active change request maps to standard, fallback, or out-of-policy position.",
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "high"
                      }
                    },
                    "errorNodeId": "1777879914368"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 5267,
                    "y": 15209
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1775380366258"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1775380208478_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a strict legal policy position matcher for contract change requests.\n\nYour task is to evaluate a contract clause change request against one policy rule and determine which policy position the change request satisfies.\n\nThe policy rule JSON is the only source of truth.\n\nDo not rely on external legal knowledge.\nDo not rely on wording similarity.\nDo not use close-enough semantic overlap.\nAll evaluation must be based on exact contractual meaning and legal effect.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nCONTRACT INTENT\n\n- BuyOrSell: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES.$output.result.BuyOrSell}}\n- If BuyOrSell = \"B\", contract intent is BUY-INTENT, and tie-breaks must favor BUYER.\n- If BuyOrSell = \"S\", contract intent is SELL-INTENT, and tie-breaks must favor SUPPLIER.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nEVALUATION PERSPECTIVE\n\nPerspective: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES.$output.result.Perspective}}\n\nEvaluate protections, obligations, qualifiers, triggers, and risk allocation relative to this perspective.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nINPUT\n\nInput Negotiation row JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem}}\n\nAuthoritative change request text (already resolved by perspective and latest non-empty side message):\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.active_change_request_text}}\n\nConversation history context (same row):\n- Latest supplier request: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.latest_supplier_change_request}}\n- Latest buyer response/request: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.latest_buyer_change_request}}\n- Supplier message timeline: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem.supplier_messages}}\n- Buyer message timeline: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem.buyer_messages}}\n- Round-wise conversation timeline: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem.round_messages}}\n\nInput Policy Rule row JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.GET_POLICY_RULE_BY_ID.$output}}\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nPOLICY STRUCTURE\n\nPositions include:\n- standard_position\n- fallback_X_position (X = 1..n)\nAdditional policy positions may exist.\n\nAssociated fields:\n- standard_clause_number, standard_risk\n- fallback_X_clause_number, fallback_X_risk, fallback_X_approval, fallback_X_approval_authority\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Only position fields (standard_position or fallback_X_position or other *_position fields) are used for classification/match.\n- Do NOT use fallback_X_clause_number, fallback_X_risk, fallback_X_approval, fallback_X_approval_authority for exact classification.\n- fallback_X_risk is used only to set severity_code after a fallback position has been selected.\n- Do NOT use fallback_X_risk to choose between multiple matching fallback positions.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTRICT LEGAL MATCHING MODE (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n\nFor each position, derive:\n1) mandatory_conditions: every obligation, limitation, qualifier, dependency, and trigger in that position.\n2) prohibited_conditions: any condition that conflicts with or weakens that position.\n3) scope_conditions: actor, timing, trigger, and boundaries (e.g., only if, unless, provided that, solely to the extent).\n\nA position matches ONLY IF:\n- every mandatory_condition is explicitly satisfied by authoritative change request text,\n- no mandatory_condition is missing, diluted, replaced, or contradicted,\n- no prohibited/conflicting/additional risk-shifting condition is introduced,\n- scope_conditions are preserved in the same legal effect.\n\nIf a position has compound qualifiers joined by and / provided / only if / subject to, ALL such qualifiers must be present.\nIf any one qualifier is missing, that position does NOT match.\n\nPartial satisfaction is NOT a match.\n\nDo NOT require exact wording matches.\n- Focus on substantive legal and commercial meaning.\n- Treat synonymous or equivalent legal phrasing as a match when the legal effect is materially the same.\n- Ignore differences in drafting style, tense, formatting, or conversational phrasing unless they materially alter risk allocation or enforceability.\n- Identify the core mandatory elements of each playbook position and determine whether those elements are preserved.\n- Do not classify as STANDARD merely because the standard's minimum requirement is satisfied.\nExample:\nStandard: \"Agreement shall be governed by California law.\"\nFallback 2: \"Agreement shall be governed by California law, with disputes resolved through neutral arbitration.\"\nCustomer: \"We can agree to California law, with disputes handled through neutral arbitration.\"\nBest Match: Fallback 2\"\n\nIf uncertain between a fallback and OUT_OF_POLICY, choose OUT_OF_POLICY.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 1 - Source Control\n\nUse conversation history only as context.\nUse ONLY authoritative change request text as the request to classify.\nDo not classify using older same-side requests when a later non-empty request exists.\nIgnore formatting-only noise during evaluation: newlines, tabs, repeated spaces, special symbols.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 2 - Evaluate All Positions For Exact Match\n\nEvaluate ALL positions (standard + all fallbacks + any other *_position fields) independently.\n\nFor each position:\n- identify mandatory_conditions, prohibited_conditions, scope_conditions\n- test authoritative change request text against all of them\n- mark as MATCH only when all conditions above are satisfied\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 3 - Determine Exact Match\n\nIdentify ALL exact matches.\n\nIf NONE match -> OUT_OF_POLICY\n\nSelection logic:\n- If standard_position matches -> return STANDARD_POSITION\n- Else if multiple fallback positions match:\n  - Do NOT select by fallback_X_risk\n  - Select the matched fallback by commercial favorability to the contract intent party:\n    - BUY-INTENT: choose the fallback more favorable to BUYER.\n    - SELL-INTENT: choose the fallback more favorable to SUPPLIER.\n  - \"More favorable\" means the position gives better rights/protections/economic outcome to the intent party (and/or imposes stronger obligations on the counterparty) for that clause topic.\n  - If still tied after favorability analysis, choose the upper fallback index (FALLBACK_2 over FALLBACK_1, etc.) for deterministic output.\n- Else return the single matched fallback\n- Never upgrade a partial/ambiguous/near match to matched fallback\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 4 - Closest Fallback Severity Override (ONLY when exact result is OUT_OF_POLICY)\n\nRun this step ONLY if STEP 3 result is OUT_OF_POLICY.\n\nClosest logic rules:\n- Try closest matching ONLY for numeric asks with one clear numeric dimension.\n- For non-numeric asks, textual asks, or ambiguous/unit-unclear extraction -> do NOT attempt closest matching.\n- Use STANDARD + all FALLBACK positions only to determine numeric boundaries (range).\n- Effective range for closest evaluation is from STANDARD anchor to the riskiest FALLBACK anchor.\n- Closest assignment must always be to a FALLBACK position only (never STANDARD).\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t   \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t  \n\nAssignment rules:\n1) If request value is between STANDARD and FALLBACK_1 (inclusive of boundary side toward FALLBACK_1), assign FALLBACK_1.\n2) If request value is between FALLBACK_i and FALLBACK_(i+1), assign the nearer of those two FALLBACK positions by numeric distance.\n3) If request value equals a FALLBACK anchor, assign that FALLBACK.\n4) If request value is beyond the riskiest FALLBACK on risky side, do NOT apply closest override.\n\n- On tie, follow below guidelines.\n\nCLOSEST FALLBACK SELECTION (when multiple fallbacks are equally close/tie condition)\n- Do NOT break ties by risk.\n- Break ties by commercial favorability to the contract intent party:\n  - BUY-INTENT: choose the fallback more favorable to BUYER.\n  - SELL-INTENT: choose the fallback more favorable to SUPPLIER.\n- \"More favorable\" means the position gives better rights/protections/economic outcome to the intent party (and/or imposes stronger obligations on the counterparty) for that clause topic.\n- If still tied after favorability analysis, choose the upper fallback index (FALLBACK_2 over FALLBACK_1, etc.) for deterministic output.\n\nOutput fields for this step:\n- closest_fallback_position_code: matched fallback code or null\n- closest_fallback_severity_code: mapped severity code from fallback_X_risk or null\n- closest_fallback_applied: true only when closest override is confidently applied, else false\n- closest_fallback_reason: short reason\n\nImportant:\n- Even when closest_fallback_applied is true, matched_position_code must remain OUT_OF_POLICY.\n- STANDARD is never a closest_fallback_position_code.\n- If a numeric request lies between STANDARD and FALLBACK_1, closest_fallback_position_code must be FALLBACK_1_POSITION.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 5 - Severity (severity_code)\n\nFor exact match path:\n- STANDARD_POSITION -> 0_NO_RISK\n- FALLBACK_X_POSITION -> fallback_X_risk\n\nFor OUT_OF_POLICY path:\n- If closest_fallback_applied = true -> severity_code = closest_fallback_severity_code\n- Else -> severity_code = 4_CRITICAL\n\nReturn severity_code in SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE using mapping:\nNo Risk -> 0_NO_RISK\nLow Risk -> 1_LOW_RISK\nMedium Risk -> 2_MEDIUM_RISK\nHigh Risk -> 3_HIGH_RISK\nCRITICAL -> 4_CRITICAL\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 6 - Issue Explanation (issue)\n\nProvide 2-3 sentences:\n- why the selected position matches (or why OUT_OF_POLICY),\n- which mandatory condition(s) were missing/violated if not standard.\n\nIf OUT_OF_POLICY with closest_fallback_applied=true, mention that only severity was aligned to the nearest fallback.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 7 - Standard Position Summary (standard_position_summary)\n\nProvide a concise 1-2 line summary of standard_position intent.\nIf standard_position is unavailable, return:\n\"No policy rule available for comparison.\"\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 8 - Change Request Summary (change_request_summary)\n\nProvide a concise 1-2 line summary of the authoritative change request intent.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nOUTPUT\n\nReturn valid JSON object only:\n\n{\n  \"policy_deviation\": {\n    \"doc_clause_title\": \"<clause_name/clause_title column value from input negotiation json>\",\n    \"issue_clause_title\": \"<clause_name/clause_title column value from input negotiation json>\",\n    \"issue_number\": <integer issue number from input negotiation json>,\n    \"clause_number\": \"<clause_number column value from input negotiation json>\",\n    \"matched_position_code\": \"<STANDARD_POSITION | FALLBACK_X_POSITION | OUT_OF_POLICY>\",\n    \"issue\": \"<Issue Explanation>\",\n    \"severity_code\": \"<0_NO_RISK | 1_LOW_RISK | 2_MEDIUM_RISK | 3_HIGH_RISK | 4_CRITICAL>\",\n    \"standard_position_summary\": \"<Standard Position Summary>\",\n    \"change_request_summary\": \"<Change Request Summary>\",\n    \"closest_fallback_position_code\": \"<FALLBACK_X_POSITION | null>\",\n    \"closest_fallback_severity_code\": \"<0_NO_RISK | 1_LOW_RISK | 2_MEDIUM_RISK | 3_HIGH_RISK | 4_CRITICAL | null>\",\n    \"closest_fallback_applied\": <true|false>,\n    \"closest_fallback_reason\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nSTRICT RULES\n\n- issue_number must be integer; if unavailable, use null.\n- Output valid JSON only (no markdown, no extra text).\n- Use policy rule JSON only.\n- No wording-similarity-only matching.\n- No partial/approximate/legal-intent-only matching.\n- Do NOT use fallback_X_clause_number, fallback_X_approval, fallback_X_approval_authority for exact classification.\n- STANDARD_POSITION severity_code must always be 0_NO_RISK.\n- matched_position_code must remain OUT_OF_POLICY for closest fallback severity override path.\n- closest fallback logic is disabled for non-numeric or ambiguous asks.\n- Do NOT omit any required output fields."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"policy_deviation\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"policy_deviation\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"doc_clause_title\",\n        \"issue_clause_title\",\n        \"issue_number\",\n        \"clause_number\",\n        \"matched_position_code\",\n        \"issue\",\n        \"severity_code\",\n        \"standard_position_summary\",\n        \"change_request_summary\",\n        \"closest_fallback_position_code\",\n        \"closest_fallback_severity_code\",\n        \"closest_fallback_applied\",\n        \"closest_fallback_reason\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"doc_clause_title\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"issue_clause_title\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"issue_number\": {\n          \"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"clause_number\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"matched_position_code\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^(STANDARD_POSITION|FALLBACK_[0-9]+_POSITION|OUT_OF_POLICY)$\"\n        },\n        \"issue\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"severity_code\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^(0_NO_RISK|1_LOW_RISK|2_MEDIUM_RISK|3_HIGH_RISK|4_CRITICAL)$\"\n        },\n        \"standard_position_summary\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"change_request_summary\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"closest_fallback_position_code\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n          \"pattern\": \"^(FALLBACK_[0-9]+_POSITION)$\"\n        },\n        \"closest_fallback_severity_code\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n          \"pattern\": \"^(0_NO_RISK|1_LOW_RISK|2_MEDIUM_RISK|3_HIGH_RISK|4_CRITICAL)$\"\n        },\n        \"closest_fallback_applied\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"closest_fallback_reason\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
                },
