                    "y": 15431
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1776064259377"
                  },
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1775380366258_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a contract clause change request recommendation generator.\n\nYour task is to compare the authoritative latest change request against each policy position in the rule JSON and generate recommendation text.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nINPUT\n\nChange Request Row JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem}}\n\nAuthoritative change request text (already resolved by perspective and latest non-empty side message):\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.active_change_request_text}}\n\nRecipient perspective:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CONTRACT_METADATA_ATTRIBUTES_VALUES.$output.result.Perspective}}\n\nActive request side:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.SELECT_ACTIVE_CHANGE_REQUEST.$output.result.active_request_side}}\n\nPolicy Rule JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.GET_POLICY_RULE_BY_ID.$output}}\n\nComplete Clause Text:\n{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.GET_THE_CLAUSE_TEXT.$output.result}}\n\nRULE\n- Use authoritative change request text only to understand intent/deviation.\n- Do NOT copy, paraphrase, or reuse change request text as recommendation_text for STANDARD/FALLBACK positions.\n- Do not use older same-side requests when a later non-empty request exists.\n- While interpreting meaning, ignore formatting-only noise: newlines, tabs, repeated spaces, and special symbols.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nPOLICY STRUCTURE\n\nPositions may include:\n- standard_position\n- fallback_X_position (X = 1..n)\n- additional policy positions\n\nAssociated fields:\n- standard_clause_number, standard_risk\n- fallback_X_clause_number, fallback_X_risk, fallback_X_approval, fallback_X_approval_authority\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nFor every position defined in the rule JSON, generate one recommendation.\n\nCore recommendation requirement:\n- If clause_number is null, recommendation_text MUST be a full revised clause text.\n- If standard_clause_number | fallback_X_clause_number exists, recommendation_text MUST be null for that position.\n- Keep the original clause text intact except the minimum required edits to fit the target position and authoritative change request.\n- Preserve all unaffected sentences, numbering, structure, and legal wording exactly.\n- Do not output edit instructions, summaries, bullets, or placeholders.\n- When rule_code is found and clause_number is null, recommendation_text MUST be generated from Complete Clause Text by applying the selected position_text edits only.\n\nCRITICAL CONSISTENCY RULE (MANDATORY):\n- If position_text changes a defined term/value (for example duration, number of days, notice period, dates, thresholds, trigger event), update ALL occurrences in the clause text that refer to the same concept.\n- Do not leave conflicting legacy values anywhere in recommendation_text.\n- If one sentence is replaced by position_text and other sentences still reference old values for that same concept, harmonize those sentences to the new value.\n- “Minimum required edits” includes all dependent cross-references needed to make the full clause internally consistent.\n\nFor STANDARD_POSITION:\n- Use standard_position as position_text.\n- Set clause_number = standard_clause_number if available, otherwise null.\n- If clause_number exists, set recommendation_text = null.\n- If clause_number is null, generate recommendation_text as full revised clause text aligned to standard_position.\n- Set severity_code = 0_NO_RISK.\n\nFor each FALLBACK_X_POSITION:\n- Use fallback_X_position as position_text.\n- Set approval = fallback_X_approval as-is.\n- Set approval_authority = fallback_X_approval_authority as-is.\n- Set severity_code = fallback_X_risk.\n- Set clause_number = fallback_X_clause_number if available, otherwise null.\n- If clause_number exists, set recommendation_text = null.\n- If clause_number is null, generate recommendation_text as full revised clause text aligned to that fallback position.\n- Modify only required portions; keep rest unchanged.\n\nUse below mapping for severity_code:\nNo Risk -> 0_NO_RISK\nLow Risk -> 1_LOW_RISK\nMedium Risk -> 2_MEDIUM_RISK\nHigh Risk -> 3_HIGH_RISK\nCRITICAL -> 4_CRITICAL\n\nAdditional policy positions, if present, must also be included in the same output format.\n\nHTML PRESERVATION RULES (MANDATORY)\n- Complete Clause Text is the source format.\n- If Complete Clause Text contains HTML tags, recommendation_text MUST preserve HTML format.\n- Do NOT convert HTML to plain text.\n- Keep existing HTML structure/tags unchanged except where minimal content edits are required by the selected position.\n- If input has no HTML, output plain text is allowed.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT\n\nReturn valid JSON only in this format:\n\n{\n  \"policy_recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"recommendation_type\": \"<STANDARD_POSITION | FALLBACK_X_POSITION | OTHER_POSITION_TYPE>\",\n      \"severity_code\": \"mapped value of fallback_x_risk | <0_NO_RISK for STANDARD_POSITION>\",\n      \"approval\": \"<fallback_X_approval or null>\",\n      \"approval_authority\": \"<fallback_X_approval_authority or null>\",\n      \"clause_number\": \"<standard_clause_number or fallback_X_clause_number or null>\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"<full revised clause text or null>\",\n      \"position_text\": \"<exact position text>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n-----------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT RULES\n\n- Output valid JSON only.\n- Do not skip any position.\n- Include recommendations for all positions in the rule JSON.\n- recommendation_type and severity_code must be in SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.\n- recommendation_text must be full clause text with just required position change only when clause_number is null.\n- Keep non-modified text identical to Complete Clause Text.\n- recommendation_text must be internally consistent with position_text across all related references."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"policy_recommendations\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"policy_recommendations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"recommendation_type\",\n          \"severity_code\",\n          \"approval\",\n\t\t      \"approval_authority\",\n          \"clause_number\",\n          \"recommendation_text\",\n          \"position_text\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"recommendation_type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"One of STANDARD_POSITION, FALLBACK_X_POSITION, or any other uppercase policy position type\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^[A-Z0-9_]+$\"\n          },\n          \"severity_code\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n            \"description\": \"Risk/severity value\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(0_NO_RISK|1_LOW_RISK|2_MEDIUM_RISK|3_HIGH_RISK|4_CRITICAL)$\"\n          },\n          \"approval\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n            \"description\": \"Fallback approval value if present, otherwise null\"\n          },\t\t  \n          \"approval_authority\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n            \"description\": \"Fallback approval authority value if present, otherwise null\"\n          },\n          \"clause_number\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n            \"description\": \"Clause number if available, otherwise null\"\n          },\n          \"recommendation_text\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n            \"description\": \"Generated recommendation text when clause_number is null; otherwise null\"\n          },\n          \"position_text\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Exact policy position text used to generate the recommendation\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
                },
                {
                  "id": "1776064259377",
                  "code": "SET_RECOMMONDATION_TEXT_FOR_CLAUSE_NUMBER",
                  "type": "CODE",
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Set Recommondation Text For Clause Number",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "description": "Adjusts recommendation text and clause-number fields using matched policy clause references.",
                    "sourceCode": "const recommendations = $context.$nodes.CR_RECOMMANDATION_GENERATOR.$output?.policy_recommendations ?? [];\nconst clauseTextMap = $context.$nodes.AGGREGATE_FETCHED_CLAUSE_TEXTS.$output?.result ?? {};\n\nconst toText = (v) => (v == null ? '' : v.toString().trim());\nconst normalizeCode = (v) => toText(v).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]+/g, '_').replace(/^_+|_+$/g, '').toUpperCase();\n\nlet mappedCount = 0;\nfor (const rec of recommendations) {\n  const recType = normalizeCode(rec.recommendation_type ?? rec.recommendationtype ?? rec.recommendationType);\n  const recText = toText(rec.recommendation_text ?? rec.recommendationtext);\n\n  // Do not overwrite LLM-generated, position-specific recommendation text.\n  // Map from clause number only when recommendation_text is empty.\n  if (!recText && rec.clause_number && clauseTextMap[rec.clause_number]) {\n    rec.recommendation_text = clauseTextMap[rec.clause_number];\n    mappedCount += 1;\n  }\n}\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  node: 'SET_RECOMMONDATION_TEXT_FOR_CLAUSE_NUMBER',\n  event: 'recommendation_text_mapped_from_clause_number',\n  issueNumber: $context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_ISSUE_IN_NEGOTIATIONS_DOC.$currentItem?.id ?? null,\n  recommendationCount: Array.isArray(recommendations) ? recommendations.length : 0,\n  mappedCount,\n  clauseTextMapSize: Object.keys(clauseTextMap || {}).length\n}));\n\nreturn recommendations;",
